+      op: '=='
+      value: 1
+  prompt: |
+    CONTEXT:
+    arXiv:2609.02817 uses a first-mistake boundary for process rewards.
+    arXiv:2609.02417 shows that targeted credit can fail when verifier coverage
+    is sparse. Carnot needs an exact fixture that measures verifier information
+    density before it trains or applies any prefix energy.
+
+    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
+
+    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
+    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md, {project_root}/CODEX.md, and
+      {project_root}/research-program.md
+    - {project_root}/python/carnot/verification
+    - {project_root}/python/carnot/constraints
+    - {project_root}/python/carnot/verify
+    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6926_span_first_relation_fixture.json
+    - {project_root}/scripts/verdict_row_consistency_lint.py
+    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/verification/spec.md
+    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md
+
+    TASK:
+    Build a deterministic line-oriented reasoning corpus with exact step
+    semantics and exact first-error labels. Measure verifier information density
+    for every trace. Include outcome-only, dense-step, sparse-step, and ambiguous
+    coverage cases. This fixture proves conformance only.
+
+    CONCRETE STEPS:
+    0. PRECONDITIONS: require v608_execution_contract_ready_score=1, current
+       exact checker interfaces, deterministic seed control, and a writable
+       checkpoint path. On failure, write blocked_verifier_density_prefix_corpus
+       with gate_check_summary.
+    1. Add REQ-VERIFY-6943 and tests first. Cover correct traces, first-line
+       errors, late errors, multiple errors, invalid syntax, missing terminal
+       states, and deterministic replay.
+    2. Create at least 144 trace pairs across arithmetic state updates, graph
+       reachability, and small scheduling constraints. Use existing exact
+       solvers or interpreters as authority.
+    3. For each valid trace, create a matched single-corruption trace. Freeze
+       corruption type, first invalid step, suffix, trace length, and split.
+    4. Emit an exact prefix-validity vector for every step. Compute verifier
+       information density k/C from observable step labels and causal-chain
+       length. Keep terminal-only cases distinct from dense cases.
+    5. Freeze calibration, held-out, and prospective-family splits by problem
+       identity. Prove no isomorphic pair crosses a split.
+    6. Replay all rows in a fresh process. Recompute the first invalid step,
+       prefix vector, final outcome, density, hashes, and split membership.
+    7. Set prefix_corpus_ready_score=1 only when all required families and
+       density bands have complete rows and fresh-process replay is exact.
+    8. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact-convention audit,
+       verdict-row consistency lint, docs audit, and root-clutter checks.
+    9. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific principle
+       per required field and prefix_corpus_ready_score; preconditions_checked;
+       inference_substrate (deterministic_exact_prefix_fixture_no_llm);
+       duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; rows; trace_rows; step_rows;
+       prefix_validity_rows; corruption_rows; domain_rows; density_band_rows;
+       split_rows; isomorphism_rows; hidden_label_isolation_rows;
+       fresh_process_replay_rows; corpus_checkpoint_path; random_seed;
+       reproducibility_checksum; prefix_corpus_ready_score; gate_check_summary
+       with failed check, expected value, and observed value for any blocked
+       verdict; verifier_is_oracle (true for fixture conformance only);
+       verdict_class (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked |
+       disqualified | partial, with circular_positive required when ready);
+       honest_verdict with a terminal prefix consistent with verdict_class.
+
